<!--
  integration/clickhouse/clickhouse/common/config.d/remote_servers.xml

  Common secret-authenticated interserver cluster definition, mounted
  identically on both clickhouse-origin and clickhouse-remote (see
  "Interserver-secret configuration" in the phase-3 plan). Both nodes need
  the same cluster/secret: the receiving node verifies the interserver
  authentication hash against this same secret, and rejects the query if
  the salt/secret is missing or does not match.

  No fixed <user>/<password> replica credentials are configured — identity
  crosses the interserver boundary via the secret plus the initiating
  username/external-role names (see "Why the remote node has the LDAP
  directory but not helper connectivity").

  The secret itself is never committed. run.sh generates a fresh value each
  run and passes it into both containers' PHASE3_CLUSTER_SECRET environment
  variable (via compose.yml, itself populated from a private, mode-0600
  per-run env file — never an exported shell variable, never a `docker -e`
  literal, never committed here).

  Contingency (see "Interserver-secret configuration" in the plan): if a
  later pinned 24.8 Altinity Stable build ever rejects `from_env` on
  <secret>, the documented fallback is to render an otherwise-identical
  temporary XML file under the runner's private $TMPDIR-rooted directory,
  with the secret value substituted in literally, and bind-mount that
  generated file over this path instead — never commit a fixed secret here.
  As of altinity/clickhouse-server:24.8.11.51285.altinitystable, `from_env`
  on <secret> was verified to work directly (single-node config-acceptance
  probe: SELECT 1 succeeds with the config below and PHASE3_CLUSTER_SECRET
  set), so that fallback is not currently exercised.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <remote_servers>
        <phase3_remote>
            <secret from_env="PHASE3_CLUSTER_SECRET"/>
            <shard>
                <replica>
                    <host>clickhouse-remote</host>
                    <port>9000</port>
                </replica>
            </shard>
        </phase3_remote>
    </remote_servers>
</clickhouse>
